2. Lida Attribution License 1.0 (LicenseRef-Lida-Attribution-1.0)
   Everything else, unless a file carries another SPDX identifier.
   See LICENSES/Lida-Attribution-1.0.txt. This includes:
   - the Unity package (unity/): shaders, HLSL, C#, asmdef, package.json,
     .meta files and documents;
   - the Unreal Engine files (unreal/): Python that uses the unreal module
     (not bpy), Custom-node text, HLSL, default PNG textures and documents;
   - the shared shading core and its tools (core/);
   - documents (README, CHANGELOG, docs/), the procedural PNG assets of the
     Blender add-on (blender/lida_angel_toon/assets/), the release tools
     (scripts/), tools/ and tests/test_*.py.
   Files that cannot carry a comment (.meta, .json, .asmdef, .png) follow the
   folder they are in.

Personal and commercial use, modification, incorporation and redistribution of
the Lida Attribution parts are allowed, also bundled with an avatar, a model, a
game or an app. When redistributing or bundling them, keep the author notice,
the license text and the source in NOTICE.md, and describe significant
modifications. The Unity package and the Unreal Engine folder carry this
information in their own LICENSE.md (unity/jp.lida.angeltoon/LICENSE.md,
